From 51c8b3040d17480d96cd939f09bb2ea6ae112622 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michele Baldessari <mbaldess@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:54:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: implement org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Clipboard
 interface

Add clipboard support for InputCapture sessions using the wlr-data-control
Wayland protocol to bridge between the XDG Desktop Portal clipboard API
and the compositor's clipboard.

The Clipboard D-Bus interface is registered on the same object as
InputCapture and implements all five required methods plus two signals:

Methods:
- RequestClipboard: flags a session for clipboard access (must be called
  before Start, i.e. with CreateSession2 flow)
- SetSelection: remote side claims clipboard ownership; creates a
  wlr-data-control source with the offered MIME types and sets it as the
  compositor's selection
- SelectionWrite: returns a pipe fd for the app to write clipboard data
  into; a detached thread forwards the data to the compositor's fd
- SelectionWriteDone: cleans up pending transfer state
- SelectionRead: reads from the current wlr-data-control offer by
  calling receive() and returning the read end of a pipe

Signals:
- SelectionOwnerChanged: emitted when a local application changes the
  clipboard (detected via wlr-data-control device selection events)
- SelectionTransfer: emitted when the compositor requests clipboard data
  from the session's data source (local app pastes)

The wlr-data-control device monitors clipboard changes and tracks the
current offer with its MIME types. When the local clipboard changes and
a clipboard-enabled session exists, SelectionOwnerChanged is emitted so
the remote side (e.g. deskflow) can read and sync the data.

The hyprland.portal file is updated to advertise the Clipboard interface
so xdg-desktop-portal knows to route clipboard operations through this
backend.
